{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-110306","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177540","text":"How a phone would fit Super's consent model — 2026-09-11"}]},{"id":"blk-110307","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177541","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: design. No write path is enabled by this document and none is built."},{"id":"spn-177542","text":" It records what the runtime already does, where a phone would attach, and what must pass before any of it is switched on."}]},{"id":"blk-110308","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177543","text":"1. What the consent model already is"}]},{"id":"blk-110309","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177544","text":"Read from source, not inferred. Four things matter and all four already exist."}]},{"id":"blk-110310","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177545","text":"1.1 Consent is bound to a digest, and the digest is already the right one"}]},{"id":"blk-110311","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177546","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Gateway.decide/4"},{"id":"spn-177547","text":" builds an "},{"id":"spn-177548","marks":["code"],"text":"approval-intent@1"},{"id":"spn-177549","text":" envelope and hashes it:"}]},{"id":"blk-110312","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"env = %{\"schema\" => \"approval-intent@1\",\n        \"effect_key\" => ek,                     # what should happen\n        \"pack\" => pack <> \"@\" <> pk[\"version\"], # which pack, which version\n        \"capability\" => cap, \"actor\" => ctx[\"actor\"], \"resource\" => resource,\n        \"grant\" => g[\"id\"], \"authority_snapshot\" => snapshot,\n        \"placement\" => pl[\"site\"],\n        \"world_installation_id\" => lin[\"installation_id\"],\n        \"world_generation\" => lin[\"generation\"],\n        \"request_id\" => er, \"request_revision\" => rev,\n        \"request\" => request[\"params\"]}\n\nh = Core.intent_digest(env)          # \"sha256:\" <> sha256_hex(canon(env))"},{"id":"blk-110313","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177550","text":"Every element of "},{"id":"spn-177551","marks":["italic"],"text":"“bind consent to the exact action, arguments, requesting agent, and version reviewed”"},{"id":"spn-177552","text":" is already inside "},{"id":"spn-177553","marks":["code"],"text":"h"},{"id":"spn-177554","text":":"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-110315","spans":[{"id":"spn-177555","text":"asked for"}]},{"id":"blk-110316","spans":[{"id":"spn-177556","text":"field in the envelope"}]}],"id":"blk-110314","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-110317","spans":[{"id":"spn-177557","text":"exact action"}]},{"id":"blk-110318","spans":[{"id":"spn-177558","marks":["code"],"text":"capability"},{"id":"spn-177559","text":", "},{"id":"spn-177560","marks":["code"],"text":"effect_key"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110319","spans":[{"id":"spn-177561","text":"arguments"}]},{"id":"blk-110320","spans":[{"id":"spn-177562","marks":["code"],"text":"request"},{"id":"spn-177563","text":" (the params), "},{"id":"spn-177564","marks":["code"],"text":"resource"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110321","spans":[{"id":"spn-177565","text":"requesting agent"}]},{"id":"blk-110322","spans":[{"id":"spn-177566","marks":["code"],"text":"actor"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110323","spans":[{"id":"spn-177567","text":"version reviewed"}]},{"id":"blk-110324","spans":[{"id":"spn-177568","marks":["code"],"text":"request_revision"},{"id":"spn-177569","text":", "},{"id":"spn-177570","marks":["code"],"text":"pack@version"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110325","spans":[{"id":"spn-177571","text":"the authority it was judged under"}]},{"id":"blk-110326","spans":[{"id":"spn-177572","marks":["code"],"text":"authority_snapshot"},{"id":"spn-177573","text":", "},{"id":"spn-177574","marks":["code"],"text":"grant"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110327","spans":[{"id":"spn-177575","text":"the world it was judged in"}]},{"id":"blk-110328","spans":[{"id":"spn-177576","marks":["code"],"text":"world_installation_id"},{"id":"spn-177577","text":", "},{"id":"spn-177578","marks":["code"],"text":"world_generation"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-110329","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177579","marks":["bold"],"text":"So the binding is not something to invent."},{"id":"spn-177580","text":" A phone consent is bound correctly exactly when it names "},{"id":"spn-177581","marks":["code"],"text":"request_hash"},{"id":"spn-177582","text":" and the host re-derives the same "},{"id":"spn-177583","marks":["code"],"text":"h"},{"id":"spn-177584","text":" at the moment of decision. "},{"id":"spn-177585","marks":["code"],"text":"Core.intent_digest/1"},{"id":"spn-177586","text":" is canonical-JSON over the whole envelope, so any change to any field produces a different "},{"id":"spn-177587","marks":["code"],"text":"h"},{"id":"spn-177588","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-110330","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177589","text":"1.2 Revision already invalidates prior consent"}]},{"id":"blk-110331","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177590","text":"When a proposal is revised, "},{"id":"spn-177591","marks":["code"],"text":"decide/4"},{"id":"spn-177592","text":" finds granted approvals with the same grant, capability and request id but a "},{"id":"spn-177593","marks":["bold"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-177594","text":" "},{"id":"spn-177595","marks":["code"],"text":"request_hash"},{"id":"spn-177596","text":", and marks each "},{"id":"spn-177597","marks":["code"],"text":"stale"},{"id":"spn-177598","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-177599","marks":["italic"],"text":"“proposal revised since consent.”"},{"id":"spn-177600","text":" Nothing about a phone changes this; a phone must simply not be able to escape it."}]},{"id":"blk-110332","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177601","text":"1.3 A world-lineage advance already expires consent"}]},{"id":"blk-110333","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177602","marks":["code"],"text":"Authority.stale_prior_consent/2"},{"id":"spn-177603","text":" marks every "},{"id":"spn-177604","marks":["code"],"text":"pending"},{"id":"spn-177605","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-177606","marks":["code"],"text":"granted"},{"id":"spn-177607","text":" approval "},{"id":"spn-177608","marks":["code"],"text":"stale"},{"id":"spn-177609","text":" when "},{"id":"spn-177610","marks":["code"],"text":"world_generation"},{"id":"spn-177611","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-177612","marks":["code"],"text":"world_installation_id"},{"id":"spn-177613","text":" moves, with the reason "},{"id":"spn-177614","marks":["italic"],"text":"“the authority state this consent was given under can no longer be re-derived.”"},{"id":"spn-177615","text":" The lineage is "},{"id":"spn-177616","marks":["bold"],"text":"inside the digest too"},{"id":"spn-177617","text":", so this falls out of the exact match rather than being a second rule that could be forgotten."}]},{"id":"blk-110334","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177618","text":"1.4 The decision command is "},{"id":"spn-177619","marks":["code"],"text":":human_control"},{"id":"spn-177620","text":", and that is the real obstacle"}]},{"id":"blk-110335","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"\"approve_effect\" => %{cmd: :approve_effect, channel: :human_control,\n  kind: :mutation,\n  fields: [%{name: \"request_id\",  type: {:id, \"er_\"}, required: true},\n           %{name: \"approval_id\", type: {:id, \"ap_\"}, required: true}]}"},{"id":"blk-110336","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177621","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/check-intent-surface.mjs"},{"id":"spn-177622","text":" holds three properties, one of which is "},{"id":"spn-177623","marks":["bold"],"text":"“every intent is exclusive to the human control channel.”"},{"id":"spn-177624","text":" A phone that issued "},{"id":"spn-177625","marks":["code"],"text":"approve_effect"},{"id":"spn-177626","text":" over a second channel would break that gate, and the gate is right: the point of the channel is that there is exactly one way a person's decision enters the world."}]},{"id":"blk-110337","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177627","text":"2. Where a phone attaches today, and what is missing"}]},{"id":"blk-110338","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177628","text":"The chain is "},{"id":"spn-177629","marks":["code"],"text":"phone → Tailscale HTTPS → connector (4320) → gateway (4318) → host"},{"id":"spn-177630","text":"."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-110340","spans":[{"id":"spn-177631","text":"layer"}]},{"id":"blk-110341","spans":[{"id":"spn-177632","text":"what it checks"}]},{"id":"blk-110342","spans":[{"id":"spn-177633","text":"strength"}]}],"id":"blk-110339","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-110343","spans":[{"id":"spn-177634","text":"connector"}]},{"id":"blk-110344","spans":[{"id":"spn-177635","marks":["code"],"text":"tailscale-user-login"},{"id":"spn-177636","text":" equals the configured owner, else "},{"id":"spn-177637","marks":["bold"],"text":"403"},{"id":"spn-177638","text":"; Host and Origin must match, else 403"}]},{"id":"blk-110345","spans":[{"id":"spn-177639","text":"a real identity, from the tailnet"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110346","spans":[{"id":"spn-177640","text":"connector"}]},{"id":"blk-110347","spans":[{"id":"spn-177641","text":"a "},{"id":"spn-177642","marks":["bold"],"text":"closed route map"},{"id":"spn-177643","text":" — three entries, snapshot/pair/logout"}]},{"id":"blk-110348","spans":[{"id":"spn-177644","text":"additions are explicit"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110349","spans":[{"id":"spn-177645","text":"gateway"}]},{"id":"blk-110350","spans":[{"id":"spn-177646","text":"session cookie, HttpOnly, same-site, 8 hours, else "},{"id":"spn-177647","marks":["bold"],"text":"401"}]},{"id":"blk-110351","spans":[{"id":"spn-177648","text":"device authentication"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110352","spans":[{"id":"spn-177649","text":"gateway"}]},{"id":"blk-110353","spans":[{"id":"spn-177650","text":"one-use pairing code, rate-limited, "},{"id":"spn-177651","marks":["code"],"text":"0600"},{"id":"spn-177652","text":", never logged"}]},{"id":"blk-110354","spans":[{"id":"spn-177653","text":"device enrolment"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110355","spans":[{"id":"spn-177654","text":"gateway"}]},{"id":"blk-110356","spans":[{"id":"spn-177655","marks":["bold"],"text":"405"},{"id":"spn-177656","text":" for every other method and path"}]},{"id":"blk-110357","spans":[{"id":"spn-177657","text":"no write surface exists"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-110358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177658","marks":["bold"],"text":"What is missing is not authentication. It is authorization at the host."},{"id":"spn-177659","text":" The gateway is a Node child with no notion of Super's authority model; a session cookie is a bearer token that says "},{"id":"spn-177660","marks":["italic"],"text":"a device paired"},{"id":"spn-177661","text":", and nothing in ampd has ever been asked whether that device may decide anything. Read-only never needed it to be."}]},{"id":"blk-110359","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177662","text":"3. The proposal"}]},{"id":"blk-110360","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177663","text":"3.1 On-demand detail, never ambient"}]},{"id":"blk-110361","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177664","text":"The ambient snapshot keeps today's narrow field allowlist — "},{"id":"spn-177665","marks":["code"],"text":"id · status · capability · actor · resource · placement"},{"id":"spn-177666","text":", no "},{"id":"spn-177667","marks":["code"],"text":"envelope"},{"id":"spn-177668","text":", no "},{"id":"spn-177669","marks":["code"],"text":"held_ctx"},{"id":"spn-177670","text":". It polls every five seconds and a phone is lost more often than a laptop, so the arguments of an unconsented effect must not sit in it."}]},{"id":"blk-110362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177671","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-177672","marks":["bold"],"text":"detail read"},{"id":"spn-177673","text":" is a separate, explicit request for "},{"id":"spn-177674","marks":["bold"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-177675","text":" approval:"}]},{"id":"blk-110363","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"GET /api/observer/approval/<ap_id>      →  connector route map (a 4th entry)\nGET /api/approval/<ap_id>               →  gateway"},{"id":"blk-110364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177676","text":"It returns the narrowed record "},{"id":"spn-177677","marks":["bold"],"text":"plus"},{"id":"spn-177678","text":" the rendered intent — the fields of "},{"id":"spn-177679","marks":["code"],"text":"approval-intent@1"},{"id":"spn-177680","text":" a person needs in order to know what they are consenting to — "},{"id":"spn-177681","marks":["bold"],"text":"plus"},{"id":"spn-177682","text":" the binding:"}]},{"id":"blk-110365","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"approval_id\": \"ap_0001\",\n  \"request_hash\": \"sha256:…\",          // what a later consent must name\n  \"world\": {\"installation_id\":\"…\",\"generation\":3},\n  \"presented_at\": \"2026-09-11T23:40:00Z\",\n  \"presentation_digest\": \"sha256:…\",   // over the exact bytes rendered\n  \"intent\": { \"capability\":\"…\", \"actor\":\"…\", \"resource\":\"…\",\n              \"placement\":\"…\", \"request_revision\":2, \"request\":{…} } }"},{"id":"blk-110366","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177683","marks":["code"],"text":"presentation_digest"},{"id":"spn-177684","text":" is hashed over "},{"id":"spn-177685","marks":["bold"],"text":"the object the phone was sent"},{"id":"spn-177686","text":", so a later consent can assert "},{"id":"spn-177687","marks":["italic"],"text":"“this is what I was shown”"},{"id":"spn-177688","text":" and the host can check that claim rather than take it. It is not a substitute for "},{"id":"spn-177689","marks":["code"],"text":"request_hash"},{"id":"spn-177690","text":"; it is the second half of the pair. "},{"id":"spn-177691","marks":["code"],"text":"request_hash"},{"id":"spn-177692","text":" says "},{"id":"spn-177693","marks":["italic"],"text":"what the runtime will do"},{"id":"spn-177694","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-177695","marks":["code"],"text":"presentation_digest"},{"id":"spn-177696","text":" says "},{"id":"spn-177697","marks":["italic"],"text":"what the person read"},{"id":"spn-177698","text":". Both must match at decision time or the decision is refused."}]},{"id":"blk-110367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177699","marks":["bold"],"text":"This is an analogy to WYSIWYS, not a citation of it."},{"id":"spn-177700","text":" What-you-see-is-what-you- sign is a digital-signature property (Landrock and Pedersen, Cryptomathic, 1998): the data-to-be-signed is rendered accurately by a trusted viewer before signing. A phone screen is not a trusted viewer and this is not a signature scheme. The useful part that does carry over is the requirement that the thing displayed and the thing authorised are provably the same object."}]},{"id":"blk-110368","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177701","text":"3.2 The phone does not issue the command"}]},{"id":"blk-110369","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177702","text":"The channel stays exclusive. The phone produces a "},{"id":"spn-177703","marks":["bold"],"text":"consent assertion"},{"id":"spn-177704","text":" — approval id, "},{"id":"spn-177705","marks":["code"],"text":"request_hash"},{"id":"spn-177706","text":", "},{"id":"spn-177707","marks":["code"],"text":"presentation_digest"},{"id":"spn-177708","text":", decision, device id, a nonce and a timestamp — and the host verifies it and issues "},{"id":"spn-177709","marks":["code"],"text":"approve_effect"},{"id":"spn-177710","text":" itself, inside the total order, on the one human-control channel that already exists."}]},{"id":"blk-110370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177711","text":"Consequences, and they are the reason to prefer this shape:"}]},{"id":"blk-110371","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177712","marks":["code"],"text":"check-intent-surface.mjs"},{"id":"spn-177713","text":" keeps holding unchanged. No second command channel."}]}],"id":"blk-110372","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177714","text":"The phone is an "},{"id":"spn-177715","marks":["bold"],"text":"authenticated authorizer"},{"id":"spn-177716","text":", not a new command issuer. The"}]}],"id":"blk-110374","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177717","text":"distinction is what keeps the 14-command allowlist meaningful."}]},{"id":"blk-110377","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177718","text":"The host is where fail-closed is enforced, so a compromised or buggy phone"}]}],"id":"blk-110378","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177719","text":"cannot skip a check by not performing it."}]},{"id":"blk-110381","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177720","text":"3.3 Fail closed, and on what"}]},{"id":"blk-110382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177721","text":"Admission is a "},{"id":"spn-177722","marks":["bold"],"text":"pure predicate over an approval record and what the phone claims"},{"id":"spn-177723","text":", so it can be tested exhaustively without a runtime. It refuses unless "},{"id":"spn-177724","marks":["italic"],"text":"all"},{"id":"spn-177725","text":" hold:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-110384","spans":[{"id":"spn-177726","text":"refusal"}]},{"id":"blk-110385","spans":[{"id":"spn-177727","text":"condition"}]}],"id":"blk-110383","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-110386","spans":[{"id":"spn-177728","marks":["code"],"text":"approval-not-found"}]},{"id":"blk-110387","spans":[{"id":"spn-177729","text":"no record with that id"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110388","spans":[{"id":"spn-177730","marks":["code"],"text":"approval-not-pending"}]},{"id":"blk-110389","spans":[{"id":"spn-177731","text":"status is anything but "},{"id":"spn-177732","marks":["code"],"text":"pending"},{"id":"spn-177733","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-177734","marks":["code"],"text":"granted"},{"id":"spn-177735","text":", "},{"id":"spn-177736","marks":["code"],"text":"denied"},{"id":"spn-177737","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-177738","marks":["code"],"text":"stale"},{"id":"spn-177739","text":" all refuse, so a resolved request cannot be re-decided"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110390","spans":[{"id":"spn-177740","marks":["code"],"text":"intent-changed"}]},{"id":"blk-110391","spans":[{"id":"spn-177741","text":"the record's "},{"id":"spn-177742","marks":["code"],"text":"request_hash"},{"id":"spn-177743","text":" differs from the one the phone names"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110392","spans":[{"id":"spn-177744","marks":["code"],"text":"presentation-mismatch"}]},{"id":"blk-110393","spans":[{"id":"spn-177745","text":"the recomputed presentation digest differs from the one the phone names"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110394","spans":[{"id":"spn-177746","marks":["code"],"text":"world-moved"}]},{"id":"blk-110395","spans":[{"id":"spn-177747","text":"the record's lineage differs from the world's now"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110396","spans":[{"id":"spn-177748","marks":["code"],"text":"presentation-expired"}]},{"id":"blk-110397","spans":[{"id":"spn-177749","text":"the presentation is older than its window"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110398","spans":[{"id":"spn-177750","marks":["code"],"text":"consent-replayed"}]},{"id":"blk-110399","spans":[{"id":"spn-177751","text":"this "},{"id":"spn-177752","marks":["code"],"text":"(approval_id, nonce)"},{"id":"spn-177753","text":" was seen before"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-110400","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177754","text":"Every one is a "},{"id":"spn-177755","marks":["bold"],"text":"refusal by name"},{"id":"spn-177756","text":". There is no default-allow branch: the predicate returns "},{"id":"spn-177757","marks":["code"],"text":"{:refused, reason}"},{"id":"spn-177758","text":" for anything it was not built to admit."}]},{"id":"blk-110401","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177759","text":"3.4 Diagnostics and logs"}]},{"id":"blk-110402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177760","text":"The detail response is the only place the arguments travel, and it must not be retained anywhere a diagnostic bundle reaches. The app's exported diagnostics already record method, path, status and elapsed — never bodies — and the connector's access log never carries a cookie, a body, a pairing code or the identity itself. "},{"id":"spn-177761","marks":["bold"],"text":"A detail response must not be added to either"},{"id":"spn-177762","text":", and the phone's screenshot path for support must not capture a detail screen."}]},{"id":"blk-110403","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177763","text":"4. What must pass before any write is enabled"}]},{"id":"blk-110404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177764","text":"Not one of these is satisfied today, and the list is the gate:"}]},{"id":"blk-110405","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177765","marks":["bold"],"text":"Authorization at the host."},{"id":"spn-177766","text":" A rule in ampd that says which device may"}]}],"id":"blk-110406","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-110408","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177767","text":"decide what, distinct from the session cookie that says a device paired. "},{"id":"spn-177768","marks":["italic"],"text":"Not designed here"},{"id":"spn-177769","text":" — it is the open question, and it is Travis's and GPT's, not a session's."}]},{"id":"blk-110409","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177770","marks":["bold"],"text":"Replay tests."},{"id":"spn-177771","text":" A consent assertion replayed after a decision, after a"}]}],"id":"blk-110410","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-110412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177772","text":"revision, after a lineage advance, and twice in a row, each refused by name."}]},{"id":"blk-110413","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177773","marks":["bold"],"text":"Staleness tests."},{"id":"spn-177774","text":" Presentation older than its window; record moved between"}]}],"id":"blk-110414","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-110416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177775","text":"presentation and decision; approval resolved in between."}]},{"id":"blk-110417","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177776","marks":["bold"],"text":"A falsifier battery."},{"id":"spn-177777","text":" Each check stubbed out in turn, the suite required to"}]}],"id":"blk-110418","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-110420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177778","text":"go red for each — the "},{"id":"spn-177779","marks":["code"],"text":"sabotage-validation.sh"},{"id":"spn-177780","text":" discipline. A check nothing can falsify is not a check."}]},{"id":"blk-110421","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177781","marks":["bold"],"text":"The ordered-boundary classification."},{"id":"spn-177782","text":" Any new ampd operation must declare"}]}],"id":"blk-110422","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-110424","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177783","marks":["code"],"text":":mutate"},{"id":"spn-177784","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-177785","marks":["code"],"text":":read"},{"id":"spn-177786","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-177787","marks":["code"],"text":":bind_basis"},{"id":"spn-177788","text":" was mis-classified for five months because nobody declared it, and the gate that would have said so was not being run."}]},{"id":"blk-110425","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177789","text":"5. What was built alongside this document"}]},{"id":"blk-110426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177790","text":"Only the predicate, and only as a pure function with its tests — items 2 and 3 above, so that the gate has something to hold. "},{"id":"spn-177791","marks":["code"],"text":"Ampd.Approvals.admit_consent/2"},{"id":"spn-177792","text":" takes an approval record and a claim and returns "},{"id":"spn-177793","marks":["code"],"text":":ok"},{"id":"spn-177794","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-177795","marks":["code"],"text":"{:refused, reason}"},{"id":"spn-177796","text":". It is called by nothing. No endpoint, no route, no command, no channel."}]},{"id":"blk-110427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177797","text":"Enabling any of this needs item 1 answered first."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieray2iokt55vqvuhzmh3fomhxmyowwrd24ko3dwyps4jxjvm3uqbjta","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}